---
description: Rules for the replay player
globs: packages/player/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Replay happens inside a sandboxed iframe. Never execute recorded scripts. Strip `<script>` and inline event handlers.
- Seeking must be fast. Use keyframes (full snapshots) so seeking never replays the whole session from zero.
- Keep rendering logic separate from React UI. The replay engine is plain TypeScript. React components only wrap it.
- The timeline, console panel and network panel all read the same current time. One source of truth.
- Large sessions (100k+ events) must stay smooth. Measure before optimizing and put numbers in the PR.
